From de5ddfc22c9bcd570d0fd60640ebf8e60bf88ee0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] feat(android): answer the desktop app's messages on a PC

With the Android app counting as the desktop app on a PC, the web UI
shows the backstage view (the File tab) and sends the messages Windows,
macOS and Qt answer natively; COOLWSD answered them with "unknown
command" errors, or nothing happened.

- COOLMessageHandler.isCODesktop() (= isDesktop()) opts in, and
  postMobileCall() answers GETRECENTDOCS with the recent documents in the
  desktop app's JSON (uri, name, timestamp, plus displayUri and doctype).
- uno .uno:Open picks a document (ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT), "opendoc" opens
  a recent one, and "newdoc" creates one from a template in the web UI's
  templates/ (or the blank one) where the user picks (CREATE_DOCUMENT);
  the new document replaces the open one, as opening from the start
  screen does. DesktopDocuments holds these for the start screen too.
- uno .uno:SaveAs saves to a place the user picks and continues there
  (the existing copy-with-TakeOwnership path).
- TEXTCLIPBOARD copies text, SETDARKMODE remembers the theme,
  FULLSCREENPRESENTATION hides the system bars during a slideshow, and
  LICENSE shows the license. The desktop-only rest (WELCOME,
  EXCHANGEMONITORS, settings sync, ...) is dropped.
- The page always gets darkTheme=true|false: the web UI keeps the last
  one it was given.

Recent documents are kept without duplicates now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
